NEARS-3640 QA — regression_bugs (pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's diff)
Device: emulator-5556, package com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_3640_edit_profile_redesign

Root cause: no android/app/google-services.json exists in this (or seemingly any fresh) worktree
checkout (it's gitignored: .gitignore:85 `**/google-services.json`; confirmed present only in the
PRIMARY tree at UserApp/android/app/google-services.json, absent from this worktree). Firebase
never initializes ("[FAIL] ... type=FirebaseInitFailure msg=\"firebase init failed
(PlatformException)\"" at app boot), so every later `FirebaseMessaging.instance` getter access
throws `[core/no-app] No Firebase App '[DEFAULT]' has been created`. Some call sites catch this
gracefully (e.g. the FCM-token-fetch path logs a proper `[FAIL] type=FcmTokenFetchFailure`); at
least two call sites do NOT and crash uncaught, both in files NEARS-3640 never touches:

1. `location_controller.dart:1129` `_saveDataAndFirebaseConfig()` calls
   `locationServiceInterface.configureFirebaseMessaging(address, ...)` BEFORE
   `AddressHelper.saveUserAddressInSharedPref(address)` (comment above it: "Commit point... past the
   availability gate the address is accepted"). `configureFirebaseMessaging`
   (location_service.dart:147-171) is not wrapped in try/catch and its first line
   (`FirebaseMessaging.instance.subscribeToTopic(...)`) throws immediately, so on a device with no
   working Firebase config THE VERY FIRST ADDRESS/LOCATION CONFIRMATION IN THE APP CAN NEVER
   COMPLETE via the normal "Pick Location"/"Use current location" flow — the address is never
   persisted and the picker screen never advances. Logcat:
     09-17 10:06:31.158 ... [INFO] msg="pick-map: saving location and navigating"
     09-17 10:06:31.159 ... [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/config/get-zone-id
     09-17 10:06:31.832 ... [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/config/get-zone-id http_status=200
     09-17 10:06:31.833 ... [INFO] msg="location: inZone=true"
     09-17 10:06:31.833 ... [ERROR:...] Unhandled Exception: [core/no-app] No Firebase App
       '[DEFAULT]' has been created - call Firebase.initializeApp()
       #3 LocationService.configureFirebaseMessaging (location_service.dart:151:25)
       #4 LocationController._saveDataAndFirebaseConfig (location_controller.dart:1133:30)
       #5 LocationController.autoNavigate (location_controller.dart:991:14)
   QA workaround used to proceed (device-local SharedPreferences write via `run-as`, per the
   nav guide's sanctioned "out-of-zone HOME" recipe — no code/config touched, no DB write):
   pre-seeded `flutter.6ammart_user_address` with a valid in-zone AddressModel JSON so the app
   skipped this broken flow entirely on next launch.

2. `auth_repository.dart:256` `AuthRepository.updateToken()` (called from
   `AuthService._updateHeaderFunctionality` during login, AFTER `saveUserToken` already persisted
   the auth token) also calls `FirebaseMessaging.instance` uncaught:
     09-17 10:11:08.193 ... [FAIL] ... type=FcmTokenFetchFailure msg="FCM registration id fetch failed"
     09-17 10:11:08.194 ... [ERROR:...] Unhandled Exception: [core/no-app] No Firebase App
       '[DEFAULT]' has been created - call Firebase.initializeApp()
       #3 AuthRepository.updateToken (auth_repository.dart:256:25)
       #6 AuthController.login (auth_controller.dart:116:37)
       #8 _SignInViewState._login (sign_in_view.dart:241:29)
   Effect: Sign In never visibly completes (stays on the sign-in screen with no error toast) even
   though the token WAS saved server-side-successfully beforehand — a force-stop + relaunch is
   needed to observe the already-completed login. This makes a plain Sign In look broken/hung with
   zero on-screen feedback.

Both call sites are confirmed OUTSIDE this ticket's diff (neither `location_controller.dart`,
`location_service.dart`, nor `auth_repository.dart` appear in
`git diff feat/human-qa-uiux...fix/NEARS-3640-edit-profile-redesign --stat`). Filed as
regression_bugs (pre-existing, unrelated) per QA process — does not affect this ticket's verdict,
but is a significant environment/product defect: on any device where Firebase is not configured,
first-run address confirmation and (invisibly) every login silently break at these two call sites.
